{{/*
  watchtower's notification body — the one message on this box that is NOT built by
  ntfy/kinds.sh, because watchtower is a container and cannot source a bash library.
  It matches the contract by hand, exactly as ntfy/system-ntfy.sh does. See
  ntfy/MESSAGES.md § 8b.

  SILENT UNLESS SOMETHING FAILED. Every other job here is silent when healthy, and
  before this watchtower sent a notification on every run that changed anything —
  which meant one a day, because tomsquest/docker-radicale:latest is rebuilt
  upstream daily. A notification you receive every day and never act on is how a
  topic gets muted, after which the one that mattered is the first thing lost.
  A successful update is deliberately invisible; `docker ps` and the image tags say
  what is running.

  THE OUTER `if .Report` IS LOAD-BEARING. watchtower renders this template for its
  STARTUP message too, where .Report is nil — without the guard that is a nil-pointer
  error in the log on every restart.

  A template that fails to parse does NOT silence watchtower: it logs
  "Could not use configured notification template, falling back to default" and
  sends the old format. Verified on this box 2026-08-22. That is the safe direction,
  but it means a broken template shows up as the OLD message rather than as no
  message — check the log if the format ever reverts.

  Plain text, not Markdown: shoutrrr's ntfy service sends without the Markdown
  header, so the escaped "1\." trick would show its backslash and is not used.
  Same reasoning as system-ntfy.sh, the other hand-matched message.
*/ -}}
{{- if .Report -}}
{{- if .Report.Failed -}}
{{- range .Report.Failed }}
{{ .Name }}
    Image: {{ .ImageName }}
    Reason: {{ .Error }}
{{- end }}

▪ {{ len .Report.Failed }} of {{ len .Report.Scanned }} containers failed
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
